-- --opens specification (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6) for CupSquare
-- (doc/cup-square.pdf): one entry per declaration, naming the definitions
-- its step reads "by definition".  Kinds as in truncation.opens and
-- circle.opens; in addition:
--   R, pt0, trans: R pt0 is Map_*(X, Omega Y) by definition (trans p refl is p);
--   two, three, four, plus, KK.K, KK.pt, KZ2, KZ4, kz2, kz4: the numerals and
--     the indexing of K(Z, m) (library aliases); K(Z,1) of the circle
--     (EM1.K1 -> TrivG.K -> img, Zab) is identified with KK.K 1 once, in e1;
--   conj-triv opens trans when comparing PiOne.comp with its body, even with
--     the common points written (checker strategy, not a step of the text).
-- Check: segd All.seg --opens cup.opens ; every line "nothing else opened".
